This is a known class of issue with Vite 8's dependency optimizer (Rolldown-based). ECharts relies on side-effectful module initialization order (e.g., `echarts/core` registering components before `echarts/charts` extends them), and the optimizer's chunking/hoisting can reorder those side effects when it pre-bundles or splits the dependency graph differently than v5's esbuild-based optimizer did.

Typical fixes to try:

```js
// vite.config.js
export default {
  optimizeDeps: {
    exclude: ['echarts'], // or include subpaths explicitly
    // or force a single bundle:
    // include: ['echarts', 'echarts/core', 'echarts/charts', 'echarts/components', 'echarts/renderers'],
  },
}
```

Also try `optimizeDeps.force: true` after clearing `node_modules/.vite`, and check whether importing from `echarts/core` + explicit `use([...])` registration (instead of the full `echarts` entry) avoids the reordering. If excluding echarts fixes it, that confirms the optimizer is the culprit and it's worth filing at github.com/vitejs/vite with a minimal repro. I'm not certain of the exact v8 regression commit, so a repro is the fastest path to a definitive answer.
